Z||000000||Songman||09-19-2000||12:06 AM||||Ogre, you pointed me to your cave about this chime box thing before. Turned out to be exactly what it was...<P>I ended up fumbling under the dash on the way home from the car show this weekend trying to find where that @%#! noise kept coming from. Finally put my hands on the little blue box and just pulled it out!<P>Now my question is... Do you or anyone else here sell the 'repaired' chime boxes? I am not technically skilled enough to do the repair you list in the cave and I'm afraid if I buy one from a salvage yard I'll have the same thing...<P>Oh yeah, can I get one that says "Turn the lights off, idiot!", "Close the door, stupid, it's cold outside!", and "Sure, just leave your keys in here. Someone would love to take me for a spin!".... Oh well, guess that would be a bit much! heheh||||reg||3
Z||000001||StuGood||09-19-2000||12:17 AM||||C'mon, guy, get a wife.<P>Just kidding.  Uh, oh, now I'm <B>really</B> in trouble    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <P>Seriously, Chrysler tried that -maybe you can adapt one of their boxes, reprogram it for ESR (enhanced sarcasm response)...<P>Nah!  Too much work... <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-19-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||Songman||09-19-2000||12:53 AM||||A wife? The when would I have the time to enjoy my Fieros?!? heheh<P>Actually, I'd just settle for a stock chime box. It really don't bother me not to have it at all, but I figured if someone has good working ones at a reasonable price that I'd stick it in there...||||reg||6
