Z||000005||286SE'S||09-19-2000||11:32 AM||||Funny you should mention that chrysler talking box. I took the one out of my brothers' girl-friends Lebaron after she wrecked it. The chime box is simple compared to the mass of wires to the talk box. Most of the wires are for sensors but a lot are for the speakers as it plays through the stereo speakers in front. Was never able to find any  information on the wiring and it ended up in the curiosity junk box.<BR>Terry<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-19-2000||11:44 PM||||Read the updated cave article which has a picture of the repair area. It's not hard to find. The whole article was reworked.<P>I'm going to look for some spare boxes at the bone yard. I may do some up just for people that are uncomfortable soldering it themselves. <P>Don't ask me a price yet. It depends what if anything they cost me. depends on time and a couple other things as well. they are small so they will likely ship thru the mail. That alone is probly 2-4$ by the time you figure you have to put them in something to ship them. Plus I still have a project in front of these I already commited to for a transmission lockup that has to be done first.<P><BR>on another note.... with current chips you can make a box that will fit the same socket and do nearly anything you want, including talk. (I hated those talking alarms.....)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bill Osmer||09-21-2000||10:53 AM||||If people want to take the time to send me their box, with return postage, I'll be glad to do the solder service for around $5 (or trade). <BR>I have already verified Ogre's fix (plus helped with photos!).  The repair has solved my intermittent problems going on 3 weeks now. Best fix yet!!<BR>BTW, I've got over 30 years oldering experience.<BR>Email me for any other details.<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||theogre||09-21-2000||02:22 PM||||<B>NOTICE!!!</B><P>It has come to my attention that there are 2(TWO) versions of chime box!<P>The Old style one has a door that opens to expose the whole back of the chime board. It is unknown at this time what if any defects apply to the old style box.(I now have one of this box for testing. I found this out while looking for spare boxes.) <P>The New style has a door that opens on the small end oposite the terminals. (It is pictured in the Fiero Tech Zone pictures.) It is this new style box that is aflicted by the defect.||||reg||1
